# 0.1.19: RAC-Board steered by the head in first person (the owner's 0.1.18 report: "hard to control. make sure it
# follows head direction"). On Novalis's start the right hand's reach gets the board out; the stick held ahead the whole
# ride. Looking ahead the heading holds; the head turned 60 degrees left, the heading comes round to the gaze and holds
# there (the view does not turn with the carve, so the gaze stays put); then 45 degrees right of where it began, the
# same; the stick let go, the board off with the left hand's reach. QUEST_JET_TRACE's lines every 15 ticks give the
# heading and the head's yaw: after each turn of the head they meet and stay met.
